{"id":9334100,"docketId":66643964,"caseName":"Daker v. Toole","caseNameFull":"Waseem DAKER v. Robert TOOLE, Warden.","slug":"daker-v-toole","docketNumber":"17-5256","dateFiled":"2017-10-02","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":2017,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":6,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":9329438,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":1709,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\"><p id=\"p-5\">Motion of petitioner for leave to proceed <em>in forma pauperis</em> denied, and petition for writ of certiorari to the United States Court of Appeals for the Eleventh Circuit dismissed. See Rule 39.8. As petitioner has repeatedly abused this Court's process, the Clerk is directed not to accept any further petitions in noncriminal matters from petitioner unless the docketing fee required by Rule 38(a) is paid and petition submitted in compliance with Rule <a class=\"page-label\" data-citation-index=\"1\" data-label=\"235\" href=\"#p235\" id=\"p235\">*235</a>33.1. See <em>Martin v. District of Columbia Court of Appeals,</em> <extracted-citation case-ids=\"11924825\" index=\"0\" url=\"https://cite.case.law/us/506/1/\"><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9432691\"><a href=\"/opinion/112790/martin-v-district-of-columbia-court-of-appeals/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Martin v. District of Columbia Court of Appeals\">506 U.S. 1</a></span></extracted-citation>, <extracted-citation case-ids=\"11924825\" index=\"1\" url=\"https://cite.case.law/us/506/1/\"><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9432691\"><a href=\"/opinion/112790/martin-v-district-of-columbia-court-of-appeals/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Martin v. District of Columbia Court of Appeals\">113 S.Ct.